==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
In other countries, frequently patterned or translated after the model of the {{w|British Labour Party}}, founded in 1900 to combine earlier centre-left parties.

===Alternative forms===
* {{sense|US, Australia}} [[Labor Party]]

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[labour|Labour]] [[party|Party]]}}

# [[any|Any]] of [[various]] [[national]] [[political parties]] [[chiefly]] [[identified]] by their [[support]] for [[organised labour]] and [[democracy]], [[particularly]] the [[British]] {{w|Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party}}.
#* '''1941''', {{w|George Orwell}}, ''{{w|The Lion and the Unicorn: Socialism and the English Genius|The Lion and the Unicorn}}'':
#*: The [[Communist]]s had considerable influence in the '''Labour Party''' in the years 1920&ndash;26 and 1935&ndash;9. Their chief importance, and that of the whole [[left wing]] of the Labour movement, was the part they played in alienating the middle classes from Socialism.
#: {{ux|en|Sure, the [[City]] loathed the old '''Labour Party''' that {{w|Jeremy Corbyn}} grew up with but they loved the [[Blairite]]s. [[New Labour]] were basically just a bunch of [[Thatcherite]] [[swot]]s who'd stayed awake through a [[branding]] seminar.}}

